# Insulin Dosing Profile

The Insulin Dosing Profile (IDP) answers the question "how do my insulin and my
glucose look together?". It puts your insulin use, your glucose and your pump
settings on one page, ready for a clinic visit.

<Video id="idp" />

## What it shows

### The key figures

The strip at the top shows your **Avg Total Daily Dose**, your **Average**
glucose, your **eHbA1c** and your **CV**. The CV target on the page is 33% or
less.

### Insulin Summary

- A bar that splits your daily insulin into basal and bolus, in units per day
  and as a percentage.
- **Avg Delivered Basal** and **Avg Scheduled Basal**, in units per day. If the
  two are different, your loop or your temp basals changed the basal from your
  schedule.
- **Boluses/Day**, **Avg Bolus Size**, **Meal Boluses/Day** and **Correction
  Boluses/Day**.

### Glucose Metrics

A bar shows how your time divides across five ranges: very low, low, in range
(70-180 mg/dL), high and very high.

### AID System Use

This card shows the devices and how much you used your automated insulin
delivery (AID) system:

- **CGM** and **Pump**: the names of your devices.
- **CGM Active** and **AID Active**: the part of the period that each one was
  active.
- **Target**: the target range from your profile.
- **Site Changes**: the number of site changes in the period.

### Glycemic Risk Index

The Glycemic Risk Index (GRI) puts the risk of lows and highs into one score,
from 0 to 100. A lower score means less risk.

The dot shows where your lows and highs put you. The horizontal axis is the part
of the risk that comes from lows. The vertical axis is the part that comes from
highs. The shaded zones run from A (0-20) to E (81-100). The panel next to the
chart shows your score and its zone.

### Glucose Pattern

This card has three charts, one under the other:

- **The glucose pattern**: your median glucose and percentile bands over 24
  hours. It is the same chart as the [AGP](/docs/reports/agp).
- **Scheduled Basal Rate**: the basal rate in your profile at each hour.
- **User-Initiated Boluses Per Day**: how many boluses you give at each hour,
  on an average day.

Under the charts, the report shows the schedules from your profile.

The app shows glucose values in mmol/L if you chose mmol/L.

## How to use it

Before a clinic visit, set the period that your care team asks for:

1. At the top of the report, select the date range.
2. Select a period, for example **30 Days**.
3. Select **Apply Filters**. The whole report loads again for that period.
4. Select **Print** to print the report.

## Good to know

- The IDP is available only to signed-in members. A public share link does not
  show it.
- If the period has too few days with readings, a badge under the figures shows
  how many days the report uses.
- **Scheduled Basal Rate** shows the first basal schedule in your profile.

<Callout type="warning" title="Talk to your care team first">

  This report is made to help your care team review your insulin doses. Do not
  change your doses or pump settings because of this report alone. Discuss
  changes with your diabetes care team.

</Callout>
